  "title": "Lincoln's Idea",
  "date": "03-13",
  "text": "Title: Lincoln's Idea\nHence his invention. Lincoln's idea was to place \"adjustable buoyant air chambers\" on the sides of any boat that would be traversing a river. Obviously inspired by the financial loss he had suffered by dumping part of his cargo on the last occasion when he had been stranded, Lincoln's patent specifically mentioned that it would enable vessels to reduce their water intake and pass over bars or shallow water \"without discharging their cargoes.\" That is because the invention, once lowered into the water, could in theory be inflated to simply lift a boat over the various obstructions.",
